WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.102
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Rachel Maddow.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking about empathy,
and I feel like one of

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:07.874 line:92%
President Biden's best qualities

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.509
insofar as what attracted voters
to him

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that he's very conciliatory
in nature,

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:15.615
which I think a lot of peopl
were looking for in this moment.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe
I'm an empathetic person.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.553
I don't know if I'm as
conciliatory as President Biden.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think that's
the right tone for this moment

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's better
than the opposite, you know?

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if we had a presiden
coming in right now

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.105
who was bent on vengeance
and hunting down those

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.807
who disagreed with him
and making sure they were

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
run out of civilized life
like some presidents I know,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.480
I think that would be a ba
thing for the country right now.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Biden --
the thing about Biden

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that everybody
knows who he is.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's been consistently
that person

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that type of politicia
his entire life.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
The country voted for someon
who they knew.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.629
And part of what they know
they're getting from him

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
is somebody who does want to b
a president for everybody,

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
who isn't out to set peopl
against each other

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to make it
the haves versus the have-nots

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.538 line:92%
and vengeance on my enemies.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I mean, I feel like
every president at the outset,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.877 size:81% position:41%
Democrat, Republican,
conservative, liberal,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:21.548 size:88% position:44%
and everything, deserves
sort of our best hopes

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our support
at the beginning.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think a lot of
my hope for Biden

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.688 line:92%
rests in that radical empathy.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.356 size:81% position:41%
I mean, he is way more
empathetic than I am,

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.326
and I feel like I have thing
to learn from him on that front,

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.461 line:92%
and I hope it serves us well

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:38.131
But there is stuff from th
Trump era that needs cleaning up

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.133
and I also hope he's going to be
able to do that.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.937
-Look, I'm not saying that COVID
was an easy problem

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
for any president to deal with
right?

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:50.410
A worldwide pandemic is, you
know, is going to test anyone.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.847
But it did seem like we were
dealing with a lack of a plan,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now there is
a plan in place.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't know
how successful it will be.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it doesn't seem
that difficult,

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
the steps that Biden
is asking us all to take.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Like, there's, you know
the very basic A-B-C

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
public-health approach
to dealing with

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
a respiratory, transmissible
potentially fatal virus.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.836
Like, it's not like they'v
invented new things to do.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just starting to d
the stuff

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.607 size:88% position:44%
that we should have done
from the very beginning.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
There ought to be a national
plan for tackling COVID.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
There ought to be
a national vaccination plan.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.314 line:92%
Trump never had one of those

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
There ought to be
a contact-tracing plan

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
and support for
implementing that.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.822
There ought to be support fo
schools who are having to change

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.291
everything about the way they do
in order to contend with this.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, all this basic stuff
that should have been

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
put in place a year ago,
Biden is now putting in plac

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:45.698 line:92%
for the first time a year late

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.635
because the only thing Trump
ever did was a travel ban.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, meanwhile,
banning people

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.972
from other countries didn't stop
us from becoming the country

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.309
with the largest death toll an
the largest epidemic on Earth.

00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:00.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I mean, I do not envy
Biden and Harris

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
the job that
they are inheriting.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:05.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I do think that one benefi
they have is that the guy

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
who they're replacing
didn't even do the easy stuff.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so they don't
have to invent

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
new complicated trickery
in order to come up with wha

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
U.S. government policy
ought to be.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.730 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's just the basics.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously a lot of
very serious things happened

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.969
during the Trump administration,
things that, as you pointed out,

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.504 line:92%
are going to take years to undo.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:27.607
With that said, do you hav
a favorite stupid scandal

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:31.077
of the Trump administratio
that only brought you joy

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.579 line:92%
that you're going to miss?

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:37.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. Like, go back to
the Trump scandal orphanag

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
and choose one?
-Yeah.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.352 line:92%
You can bring one with you

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I would love if
a President Biden also, like

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.758 line:92%
used a Sharpie to adjust maps.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.827 line:92%
I think that was a fun thing

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think enough president
have done that,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.931
and I think that should be a
thing presidents do from now on.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember --
Well, okay, it's a tie.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, Trump had
the Interior Secretary guy

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had a flag made for himsel
that every time

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.309
he was in the Interior Secretary
headquarters,

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.813
a staffer would have to run up
to the roof and fly his standard

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:11.951
to alert the peasantry that th
Interior Secretary was there

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.719 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That was pretty good.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then there was also
the EPA guy --

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't even remember
his name --

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:23.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
who built a super secure
"Get Smart" spy telephone boot

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:27.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
in his office so he could have
uber top secret

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
EPA conversations
with the White House.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was --
and then he had, like --

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
he hired himself
a 24/7 security guard,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:39.379
and things that turned up on
the, like, reimbursement sheet

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:46.352
were things like ballistic pants
for his EPA security team

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know,
would keep him safe

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he was going
into the phone booth.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:52.425
-I feel like every Cabinet
member for the next like

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
three months is going to
keep reporting back like, "Hey

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:58.531
do you know there's a solid gold
microwave in my office?"

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That's right.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that'll at least be
something to look forward to

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.704 line:92%
Have a great day tomorrow.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:08.207
Very happy you'll be covering it
live throughout the day.

